        {
          "kicker": "Build-up buzz",
          "heading": "Hosting Ireland in Suva would be 'nothing greater' for Fiji",
          "body": "Build-up coverage puts a Suva fixture above all else, though it does not say who made the remark. The idea is a pointed one given the summer Fiji have had: their Nations Championship \"home\" games were played on UK soil because of commercial considerations, with the national stadium not considered of a suitable standard to host regular Test matches. Fiji go into Saturday's trip to Dublin having lost 54-17 to France in Lyon."
        },
