    "387": {
      "date": "2026-11-14",
      "edition": "Saturday 14 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Hard-fought win",
          "heading": "Antoine Dupont inspires France past Springboks 21-19, ending five-match losing run",
          "body": "France held on for a 21-19 win over South Africa at Stade de France, ending a five-match losing run against the world champions. Tries from Aaron Grandidier-Nkanang, Theo Attissogbe and Louis Bielle-Biarrey came in a frantic first half, and Antoine Dupont was named player of the match. South Africa number eight Jasper Wiese was shown a red card early in the second half, and Manie Libbok then missed the conversion that would have levelled the game. The win leaves France six points clear in the northern hemisphere standings."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Beauden Barrett replaces Codie Taylor as All Blacks captain",
          "body": "Tadhg Beirne named Ireland captain for Fiji game. Wales' Aaron Wainwright misses New Zealand Test through injury. Wallabies recall Carter Gordon at flyhalf after broken leg."
