      "edition": "Saturday 14 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Selection call",
          "heading": "Tadhg Beirne named Ireland captain as Andy Farrell makes seven changes",
          "body": "Andy Farrell has made seven changes for Saturday's meeting with Fiji at the Aviva Stadium, with lock Tadhg Beirne captaining Ireland in a home game for the first time. Mack Hansen moves to fullback, Hugo Keenan drops out of the matchday 23, and Jamie Osborne and Bundee Aki form an all-new centre partnership. Dan Sheehan is stood down for 12 days with concussion, so Rónan Kelleher comes into the front row, and James McNabney is set to debut from the bench."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Beauden Barrett replaces Codie Taylor as All Blacks captain",
